.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH nut-doctor 1  "nut-cli 0.1.0" nut
.SH NAME
nut\-doctor \- Check UPS protection and recovery readiness
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnut doctor\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-observe\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-S\fR|\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-ups\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-upsd\-address\fR] [\fB\-\-upsd\-port\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fICHECK\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check UPS protection and recovery readiness
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output policy
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-observe\fR \fI<SECS>\fR
Run additional stability observations for this many seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII symbols and bars
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-strict\fR
Treat warnings as failures
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON where supported
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
List the check catalog without running checks
.TP
\fB\-\-ups\fR \fI<UPS>\fR
UPS name (defaults to the selected host configuration, or `cp1500`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Include additional diagnostic detail
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read host settings from this file
.TP
\fB\-\-upsd\-address\fR \fI<ADDRESS>\fR
Loopback upsd address (defaults to 127.0.0.1)
.TP
\fB\-\-upsd\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Loopback upsd port (defaults to 3493)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fICHECK\fR]
Check IDs or section prefixes
